Yes. This is a major feature, and I would make it a dedicated module called AI Schematic & PCB Intelligence Scanner inside AutoElectric Lab Pro.

The idea is that a technician uploads an actual automotive ECU schematic, PCB layout, or clear photograph of a circuit board. The system analyzes the image, identifies components and their reference designators, maps connections, creates interactive overlays directly on the original image, and allows technicians to select components, trace electrical paths, inspect information, and perform virtual electrical tests.

There is one important engineering distinction: a schematic, a PCB layout and a photograph of a physical PCB are different sources of information. The scanner must recognize which one it is analyzing. It must never invent hidden PCB connections, component values, or internal circuit paths that cannot be established from the supplied material.

We can make this extremely powerful, but no AI vision system can honestly guarantee 100% accuracy on every uploaded image. The prompt below makes verification, traceability and uncertainty handling mandatory.

